{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And if a man sell his daughter to be an amah.</b> The Torah granted the father permission to sell his daughter when she is a minor. <br><b>She shall not go out as the slaves go out.</b> She shall not go out as Canaanite slaves go out, who go out by tooth and eye. Whenever we find 'slaves' or 'slave and amah' without specification, the text speaks of Canaanites, for concerning the Hebrew slave it is explicitly stated: ״כי תקנה עבד עברי״. And this prohibition falls upon the master: if he seeks to release her from his possession by tooth and eye, he transgresses this negative commandment; rather, he must pay her the value of the tooth and the eye, and she remains with him for designation until the appointed time."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:02:08.559505525Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}